  "notes": "Night sky throughout; two paths for «ضلالا بعيدا» only. The hypocrites' sworn excuse «إن أردنا إلا إحسانا وتوفيقا» is not glossed (it would read as a fact); 62:9-11 says only that they came making excuses. STAGING v4: 60: the hypocrites (a people group) in a town; speak on 60:5 (their claim of faith), turn away on 60:15 and walk off on 60:17 (seeking judgement elsewhere); the taghut is not drawn; Satan only as the two-paths plate. 61: when called (passive, no caller drawn; door plate on 61:4) they turn away and walk off (61:13-14) and leave the stage on 61:15, well before 62. 62: the empty street with a gust of wind on 62:4; they are never shown coming to anyone or swearing (nothing implies the Prophet). The Prophet is never drawn."
